# RNNoise models are plain ASCII, so Git for Windows (core.autocrlf true) checked them out
# with CRLF line endings. Their bytes then missed the SHA-256 pins in modules/filters.py
# (ARNNDN_MODEL_SHA256), and the first arnndn_speech run deleted the bundled model and
# downloaded it again (offline: failed). They are data, never text.
*.rnnn binary
